<ShaderNodePreset Name="Guided Matte" ShaderType="Matchbox" Version="0.4" SoftwareVersion="2025.2.3" CommercialUsePermitted="True" Description="Guided Matte refines a rough matte using colour detail from a guide image, usually the original plate. The full RGB guided filter follows colour boundaries, including edges with similar luminance.&#10;&#10;Connect the original plate to Guide / Plate and a monochrome mask to Rough Matte. Blur Width is like a search range, and Edge Detail controls the detail frequency to include.&#10;&#10;Based on Rafael Silva’s **rs_GuidedBlur 1.3** Nuke gizmo, which in turn was based on *Guided Image Filtering* by Kaiming He, Jian Sun and Xiaoou Tang (ECCV 2010). Big thanks to Rafael for the original tool.&#10;&#10;Flame version by **Nils Crompton**  &#10;Questions or bugs: **[hello@nilscrompton.com](mailto:hello@nilscrompton.com)**&#10;&#10;**Version 0.4.** Aimed at Flame 2025.2.3 and up. Compiler checks have passed on Mac in 2025.2.3 and 2026.2.2; an earlier build also passed in 2025.2.5. Linux hasn’t been tested yet, and matching results across versions still needs a visual check.&#10;&#10;Shared under [MIT](https://opensource.org/license/mit), with the upstream [BSD-2-Clause](https://opensource.org/license/bsd-2-clause) notices kept in the source. Commercial use and modifications are welcome—please keep the licence notices with it. The full texts are included in the GLSL files." MatteProvider="True" SupportsAction="False" SupportsTimeline="False" SupportsTransition="False" SupportsAdaptiveDegradation="False" LimitInputsToTexture="True" TimelineUseBack="False">
